 36CA2c  via the two-step fragmentation with a E=95 MeV/nucleon primary {+40}Ca 
 36CA3c  beam incident on a 400 mg/cm{+2} carbon foil. The secondary target was 
 36CA4c  a 198 {I10} mg/cm{+2} thick {+9}Be foil. The reaction products were    
 36CA5c  analyzed with the SPEG spectrometer and detected by a scintillator at  
 36CA6c  the focal plane of SPEG. |g rays were detected with the Chateau de     
 36CA7c  Crystal array of 74 BaF{-2} detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, particle-|g  
 36CA8c  coin, particle momentum distributions. Deduced levels, cross sections. 
 36CA9c  Comparisons with Monte-Carlo simulations and shell-model calculations. 
